  "articleBody": "It's a scary moment when your child gets arrested, and it's totally normal to feel overwhelmed. The juvenile justice system works differently than the adult system, focusing more on rehabilitation than just punishment. First, your child might be released to you or held in a juvenile hall. Then, a probation officer will review the case and decide whether to file a petition with the court, which is similar to a criminal complaint. They'll consider factors like the severity of the offense, your child's past record, and family circumstances. An attorney can step in early to advocate for your child, helping navigate these initial stages and working to ensure their rights are protected and the best possible outcome is pursued. Remember, early intervention is key when dealing with juvenile charges.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}